{
  "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8062-97dd-fbe53495315a",
  "title": "RESTful Web Services with @RestController and @RequestMapping",
  "sourceUrl": "https://xpandeyed.notion.site/20824eb1ed54806297ddfbe53495315a",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80cc-90e9-fc75afb70567",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80f3-895f-cedd8bbf3ffd",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "RESTful Web Services with @RestController and @RequestMapping"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8012-a2f9-f462a8fef359",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "1. Core Concept"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8076-8edd-fcf5ca4b84b2",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "RESTful web services are a way to build web APIs that communicate over HTTP using standard HTTP methods like GET, POST, PUT, DELETE."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8092-9f72-d03f983673e0",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "In Spring Boot, "
        ],
        [
          "@RestController",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " is a specialized class annotation that simplifies creating these APIs by automatically handling HTTP responses, and "
        ],
        [
          "@RequestMapping",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " (and its variants) maps specific URLs and HTTP methods to Java methods. This makes it easy to build web services that clients (like browsers or apps) can call to perform operations or get data."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8030-b763-eb1fd5d4ec98",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80e8-a52c-f69f30d2308b",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "2. Key Interview Points"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8046-9313-d0ed074af223",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "What is ",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "@RestController",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ],
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "?",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8021-82d6-c4cae58b13d9",
          "type": "text",
          "richText": [
            [
              "It’s a combination of "
            ],
            [
              "@Controller",
              [
                [
                  "c"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              " and "
            ],
            [
              "@ResponseBody",
              [
                [
                  "c"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              ". It tells Spring that this class will handle HTTP requests and that the returned objects should be automatically converted to JSON or XML and sent as the HTTP response body."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-805e-b328-e2b2b6e36896",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Role of ",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "@RequestMapping",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ],
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " and its variants (",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "@GetMapping",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ],
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", ",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "@PostMapping",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ],
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", etc.)",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "20824eb1-ed54-806c-806b-e9b875dbec74",
          "type": "text",
          "richText": [
            [
              "These annotations map HTTP requests to specific handler methods based on URL paths and HTTP methods (GET, POST, etc.)."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80ed-a376-ea19d39e1de9",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "How Spring Boot converts Java objects to JSON/XML (Message Converters)",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80f7-a41b-e3b75a11b3b1",
          "type": "text",
          "richText": [
            [
              "When you return an object from a "
            ],
            [
              "@RestController",
              [
                [
                  "c"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              ", Spring uses built-in converters (like Jackson for JSON) to serialize that object into the appropriate format automatically."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8056-8203-e8d0b76b3473",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Difference between ",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "@Controller",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ],
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " and ",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "@RestController",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ],
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "20824eb1-ed54-800e-9335-cd61a5b86382",
          "type": "text",
          "richText": [
            [
              "@Controller",
              [
                [
                  "c"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              " is used for MVC apps where the method returns views (like JSP pages), whereas "
            ],
            [
              "@RestController",
              [
                [
                  "c"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              " is used for REST APIs where the method returns data directly."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8070-9c65-c3722c209a98",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80fa-ba21-d5197ace7f86",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "3. Code Example"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8078-9e81-e4d0eafd27d2",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Here’s a simple Spring Boot REST controller to manage “users”:"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-804d-b9fb-ce2ed75676ad",
      "type": "code",
      "richText": [
        [
          "import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;\n\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n@RestController\n@RequestMapping(\"/users\")  // Base URL for all endpoints in this controller\npublic class UserController {\n\n    private List<String> users = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    @GetMapping\n    public List<String> getAllUsers() {\n        return users;  // Return all users as JSON array\n    }\n\n    @PostMapping\n    public String addUser(@RequestBody String user) {\n        users.add(user);  // Add user sent in request body\n        return \"User added: \" + user;\n    }\n\n    @GetMapping(\"/{id}\")\n    public String getUserById(@PathVariable int id) {\n        if (id < 0 || id >= users.size()) {\n            return \"User not found\";\n        }\n        return users.get(id);\n    }\n}\n"
        ]
      ],
      "language": "Java"
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8098-a9d3-cc46a3afdb18",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "What’s happening here?",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80c0-a122-cb5f51c862a2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@RestController",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " marks the class as a REST API handler."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8056-ae40-c08f4261601b",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@RequestMapping(\"/users\")",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " sets a base path for all methods."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8063-b340-f27191adbe26",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@GetMapping",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " handles HTTP GET to "
        ],
        [
          "/users",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " and returns the list of users as JSON."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8023-b7d3-ffbd9806a2a5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@PostMapping",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " handles HTTP POST to "
        ],
        [
          "/users",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " and adds a new user from the request body."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80de-aeab-d506e252615c",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@GetMapping(\"/{id}\")",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " handles GET requests with a path variable to get a specific user."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8075-8897-fade6a5b5e98",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80c7-8684-ef76e59176b3",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "4. Common Interview Questions"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
